\begin{note}
The \lstinline{functools.lru_cache} decorator is a library implementation of memoization.
It uses the arguments to the decorated function as the dictionary keys,
so the arguments must be \emph{hashable}.
Mutable containers like lists and dicts are not hashable,
and passing them to an \lstinline{lru_cache}'d function raises \lstinline{TypeError}.
\end{note}
